%% UC-15 — Register device & receive push notifications
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant F as Flutter App
    participant FCM as Firebase Cloud Messaging
    participant B as Backend (participantRouter)
    participant M as MongoDB

    F->>FCM: Request device token (firebase_messaging)
    FCM-->>F: fcmToken
    F->>B: POST /api/v1/participant/register-token {fcmToken}
    B->>M: Store token for userId
    B-->>F: 200 registered
    Note over B,FCM: Later: researcher campaign (UC-24) targets this user, or the<br/>habit-creation check-in push fires (data: {type: "srhi", screen: "habits",<br/>intentionId}, see UC-13/UC-35)
    B->>FCM: send(message, tokens, data: {screen})
    FCM-->>F: Push notification delivered
    F->>F: routeFromNotificationPayload(data): screen "habits" -> /habits<br/>(My Habits), "questionnaire" -> /settings/profile (My Profile),<br/>"explore" -> /explore, default -> /share
    F->>F: GoRouter.go(route) via getInitialMessage()<br/>(cold start) / onMessageOpenedApp (background)

    Note over F: The "Questionnaire ready" LOCAL reminder (non-SRHI due questionnaires,<br/>reminder_scheduler_service.dart) is a separate mechanism from FCM above — it's<br/>scheduled on-device via flutter_local_notifications, not sent through this<br/>backend. Its payload is a fixed "/settings/profile" route, wired through<br/>onDidReceiveNotificationResponse / getNotificationAppLaunchDetails(). See<br/>UC-33 for the habit-reminder local notification, which instead routes to<br/>"/habits".
